{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01RR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0005": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0006": "$(U, f)$", "MATH_0007": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0008": "$x \\in U$", "MATH_0009": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0010": "$\\varphi$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-domain-of-definition}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1c1a5486c9f0591198e29d935c9b7bccd1fec475e52ac35b850cea37d3bf4511", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fcc8ff98de301ae55ac7ec8d9a4e8f164e63d949350cf099d0dcfe9a52f0a4de", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a rational map between two schemes <MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003>. We say\n<MATH_0004> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>defined in a point <MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if there exists a\nrepresentative <MATH_0006> of <MATH_0007> with <MATH_0008>. The\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>domain of definition<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> of <MATH_0009> is the set of all points\nwhere <MATH_0010> is defined.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:434427596ab8089b3f604fb79e456d1b0d43d7b781853e1e860e4c729201d04b", "unit_id": "tag:0A1X:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01RR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\varphi$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f78ef4c5711908fbe9e0698d602d3fd3adf324fbdc54cd623ecf75839f2aeb98", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:88fc75ac35b1c707d40abdc359fc5e8013054dc791827d8622de083d3d482e66", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWith this definition it isn't true in general that <MATH_0001> has a\nrepresentative which is defined on all of the domain of definition.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:98d646f8cb5ec79be057ec8deb49b4db1a5bc10b7a9de4999e911b154d5106f6", "unit_id": "tag:01RR:prose-0006"}
